.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MK.DELAYLOAD.MK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk.delayload.mk
.Nd loads a shared library at its first call, on Windows
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A delay-loaded DLL is loaded at the first call into it, not when the program
starts, so the program can start without it.
A library declares the default, and a module linking it can override that for
itself.
.Pp
Not included directly by a makefile.
.Ss Variables
.Bl -tag -width "DELAYLOAD.lib"
.It Va DELAYLOAD
On a shared library:
.Cm yes
or
.Cm no ,
the default.
.It Va DELAYLOAD. Ns Ar lib
On a program or shared library linking
.Ar lib :
.Cm yes
or
.Cm no ,
replacing that library's default.
.El
.Pp
How, by output:
.Bl -tag -width "mingw-w64, GNU ld" -offset indent
.It MSVC, cl.exe or clang
.Fl Wl,--delayload ,
turned into
.Ql /DELAYLOAD
with
.Pa delayimp.lib
.It mingw-w64, ld.lld
.Fl Wl,--delayload
.It mingw-w64, GNU ld
a delay-import library,
.Pa lib Ns Ar name Ns Pa .delay.a ,
made with
.Xr dlltool 1
from the DLL's
.Pa .def
.It anything else
nothing: a library's default has no effect, and a consumer's
.Cm yes
prints a note and links normally
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "lib/libNAME.delayload"
.It Pa lib/lib Ns Ar name Ns Pa .delayload
written by the library:
.Ar default dll data ,
where
.Ar dll
is
.Fl
if there is none, and
.Ar data
is 0, 1, or
.Ql \&?
if unknown
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# libfoo.m/makefile
LIB=foo
DELAYLOAD=yes
\&.include <mk.lib.mk>

# app.m/makefile
PROG=app
LIBS=foo bar
DELAYLOAD.foo=no
DELAYLOAD.bar=yes
\&.include <mk.prog.mk>
.Ed
.Pp
A missing DLL ends the program at the first call with exit status 127 and no
message.
Bmake It links no code of its own into what it builds; for a message, define the
toolchain's failure hook in the program:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <windows.h>
#include <delayimp.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
static FARPROC WINAPI on_failure(unsigned reason, PDelayLoadInfo info) {
    (void)reason;
    fprintf(stderr, "cannot load %s\en", info->szDll);
    exit(1);
}
#ifdef _MSC_VER
const
#endif
PfnDliHook __pfnDliFailureHook2 = on_failure;
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It DELAYLOAD= Ns Ar value : expected yes or no
A bad value.
.It DELAYLOAD=yes on the static library Ar lib
Only a shared library can be delay-loaded.
.It DELAYLOAD. Ns Ar lib Ns =yes on the static library Ar name
A static library links nothing; set it on what links that library.
.It DELAYLOAD. Ns Ar lib is set in Ar module , but Ar lib is not in its LIBS=
Probably misspelt.
.It Ar dll exports data , and a DLL that exports data cannot be delay-loaded
Export functions only, or do not delay it.
.It there is no lib Ns Ar lib Ns .delay.a
An imported DLL under GNU ld, which has no
.Pa .def
to make one from.
Use ld.lld or the MSVC linker.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dlltool 1 ,
.Xr mk.lib.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.prog.mk 5 ,
.Xr bmake-it 7
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Sylvain Souche
.Sh CAVEATS
It covers the direct link only: a library's own dependencies follow their own
settings.
A misspelt
.Va DELAYLOAD. Ns Ar lib
is noticed only in the module's own makefile, because
.Xr make 1
cannot list variables.
For an imported DLL, data exports are unknown; ld.lld and the MSVC linker refuse a
data import themselves.
